During 2023, Northrop Grumman's Stock-based Compensation Expense adjustment was **$87 million**.

This figure appears in the Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows under "Adjustments to reconcile to net cash provided by operating activities," where it is added back to net earnings (being a non-cash expense). The adjustment reconciles net earnings of $2,056 million to net cash provided by operating activities of $3,875 million.

For context, the stock-based compensation expense for the prior two years was $99 million in 2022 and $94 million in 2021. This information is also confirmed in Note 14 of the 10-K filing (Stock Compensation Plans and Other Compensation Arrangements), which states: "Stock-based compensation expense for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2022 and 2021 was $87 million, $99 million and $94 million, respectively."

