**Answer:** The adjusted net income of Genuine Parts Company for the six months ended June 30, 2019 **decreased by 0.6%** compared to the prior year period (six months ended June 30, 2018).

**Supporting Details:**

The adjusted net income figures, as disclosed in the reconciliation table in the Q2 2019 Form 10-Q (filed July 19, 2019, and amended by the Form 10-Q/A filed August 9, 2019), are:

| Period | Adjusted Net Income |
|---|---|
| Six Months Ended June 30, 2019 | $417,479 thousand ($417.5 million) |
| Six Months Ended June 30, 2018 | $420,012 thousand ($420.0 million) |

The Management's Discussion and Analysis section of the report explicitly states: *"Adjusted net income for the six months ended June 30, 2019, which also excludes the impact of realized currency losses, was $417.5 million, a decrease of 0.6% for the same six month period of 2018."*

**Calculation verification:** (417,479 − 420,012) ÷ 420,012 × 100 = −0.60%.

The adjustments to arrive at adjusted net income include the exclusion of $27.0 million in realized currency losses, $11.2 million in transaction and other costs, and the related tax impacts totaling $(5.4) million for the six months ended June 30, 2019. For the prior year period, adjustments excluded $22.1 million in transaction and other costs with a tax impact of $(5.7) million.

**The "report dated August 9, 2019"** refers to the Form 10-Q/A (Amendment No. 1 to the Quarterly Report on Form 10-Q for the period ended June 30, 2019), filed with the SEC on August 9, 2019. While this amendment primarily addressed a correction in the "Controls and Procedures" section and did not alter the financial statements, the adjusted net income data and percentage comparison are part of the amended quarterly report that this filing relates to.

