### May 2019 8-K — Reconciliation Requirement for Non-GAAP Financial Measures

The May 2, 2019 Form 8-K for Expedia Group, Inc. (NASDAQ: EXPE) included the following reconciliation requirement under **Item 2.02 (Results of Operations and Financial Condition)**:

> "Expedia Group is making reference to non-GAAP financial measures in both the earnings release and the conference call. **A reconciliation of these non-GAAP financial measures to the nearest comparable GAAP financial measures is contained in the attached Exhibit 99.1 earnings release.**"

This is a standard disclosure requirement under SEC Regulation G and Item 10(e) of Regulation S-K, which mandates that whenever a registrant publicly discloses non-GAAP financial measures, it must also present the most directly comparable GAAP financial measure and a reconciliation of the differences between the two.

---

### May 2020 Investment Agreements — Non-GAAP Adjustments

**No similar non-GAAP adjustments were detailed in the May 2020 Investment Agreements or the related 8-K filings.** 

The Investment Agreements were disclosed in the Form 8-K filed on May 5, 2020 (and initially on April 23, 2020). These agreements concerned the sale of Series A Preferred Stock and Warrants to purchase Common Stock to affiliates of Silver Lake Group, L.L.C. (SLP Fort Aggregator II, L.P. and SLP V Fort Holdings II, L.P.) and AP Fort Holdings, L.P. (an affiliate of Apollo).

After reviewing all May 2020 8-K filings (May 5, May 18, and May 20, 2020) as well as the April 23-24, 2020 8-Ks that initially set forth the Investment Agreements:

- The May 5, 2020 8-K (which completed the Investment Agreement transactions) contained no non-GAAP financial measures, no reconciliation requirements, and no non-GAAP adjustments related to the Investment Agreements.
- The term "consolidated EBITDA" did appear in the May 5, 2020 8-K, but solely in the context of **Credit Facility Amendments** (a separate agreement), not the Investment Agreements. This related to a leverage ratio covenant calculated on an annualized basis.
- The May 18, 2020 8-K (segment recast) contained a standard non-GAAP reconciliation statement similar to the May 2019 filing, but this was related to a segment reporting update and earnings release, not the Investment Agreements.
- The April 23, 2020 8-K containing the original Investment Agreements defined terms related to the preferred stock (dividend rate, preference amount, etc.) but did not include any non-GAAP financial measures or adjustments.

**In summary:** While the May 2019 8-K explicitly noted that a reconciliation of non-GAAP financial measures to GAAP measures was provided in the earnings release exhibit, no comparable non-GAAP adjustments or reconciliation requirements were detailed in the May 2020 Investment Agreements themselves.

