Because the actual Operating ROE of 10.6% fell below the 12.4% target (but above the 5.4% threshold), the earn-out multiplier for the Operating ROE portion of the 2022 PSU awards was 80.7%, determined by straight-line interpolation between the threshold (5.4% → 25% multiplier) and target (12.4% → 100% multiplier).

**Miss by: 180 basis points**

Sources:
- Everest Group, Ltd. 2023 Proxy Statement (DEF 14A), filed April 14, 2023 — details the 2022 PSU target measures including the 12.4% Operating ROE target performance scale (threshold: 5.4% at 25%, target: 12.4% at 100%, maximum: ≥17.4% at 175%) and the actual 2022 Operating ROE result of 10.6% with an 80.7% award multiplier.
- Everest Group, Ltd. 2024 Proxy Statement (DEF 14A), filed April 12, 2024 — confirms the 2022 Operating ROE actual of 10.6% vs. the 12.4% target.

