## Oracle Corporation: Adjusted Diluted EPS Guidance vs. Actual Results (FY2019–FY2020) and FY2021 Guidance

### Background
Oracle's fiscal year ends May 31. So FY2019 covers June 2018–May 2019, FY2020 covers June 2019–May 2020, and FY2021 covers June 2020–May 2021. Oracle typically provides next-quarter Non-GAAP (Adjusted) Diluted EPS guidance in each quarterly earnings press release.

---

### FY2019 Results: Oracle Surpassed Guidance in All 4 Quarters (100%)

| Quarter | Guidance Range | Actual Adjusted Diluted EPS | Result |
|---------|---------------|------------------------------|--------|
| Q1 FY2019 (Aug 2018) | $0.67 – $0.69 | $0.71 | **Surpassed** |
| Q2 FY2019 (Nov 2018) | $0.77 – $0.79 | $0.80 | **Surpassed** |
| Q3 FY2019 (Feb 2019) | $0.83 – $0.85 | $0.87 | **Surpassed** |
| Q4 FY2019 (May 2019) | $1.05 – $1.08 | $1.16 | **Surpassed** |

**FY2019 Summary:** 4 out of 4 quarters surpassed guidance.

---

### FY2020 Results: Oracle Met Guidance in Most Quarters

| Quarter | Guidance Range | Actual Adjusted Diluted EPS | Result |
|---------|---------------|------------------------------|--------|
| Q1 FY2020 (Aug 2019) | $0.80 – $0.82 | $0.81 | **Met** (within range) |
| Q2 FY2020 (Nov 2019) | $0.88 – $0.90 | $0.90 | **Met** (at high end) |
| Q3 FY2020 (Feb 2020) | $0.95 – $0.97 | $0.97 | **Met** (at high end) |
| Q4 FY2020 (May 2020) | $1.20 – $1.24 | $1.20 | **Met** (at low end) |

**FY2020 Summary:** 0 out of 4 quarters strictly surpassed guidance; all quarters fell within the guided range.

---

### FY2021 Guidance Projection
In its Q4 FY2020 earnings release (issued June 16, 2020), Oracle provided the following initial guidance for FY2021:

- **Q1 FY2021 Adjusted Diluted EPS Guidance:** $0.85 – $0.89 (constant currency)
- Oracle also indicated expectations for continued revenue and earnings growth driven by its cloud infrastructure and autonomous database businesses. As the year progressed, Oracle raised its guidance incrementally each quarter, ultimately delivering full-year FY2021 Non-GAAP diluted EPS of approximately $4.67, representing double-digit growth over FY2020.

