The difference in basis points depends on which BK senior note tranche is being referenced, as BK issued multiple tranches on July 15, 2024 (trade date). Here is a breakdown:

### Bank of New York Mellon (BK) — Senior Notes (Trade Date: July 15, 2024, Settlement: July 22, 2024)

BK issued three tranches of **Senior Medium-Term Notes, Series J**:

| Tranche | Amount | Coupon | Maturity | Spread Over Benchmark | Benchmark |
|---------|--------|--------|----------|----------------------|-----------|
| 4.890% Fixed/Floating Senior Notes | $600M | 4.890% | July 21, 2028 | **+65 bps** | UST 4.375% due July 15, 2027 |
| Floating Rate Senior Notes | $300M | SOFR + 0.83% | July 21, 2028 | **+83 bps** | Compounded SOFR |
| 5.060% Fixed/Floating Senior Notes | $1,100M | 5.060% | July 22, 2032 | **+90 bps** | UST 4.250% due June 30, 2031 |

BK also issued one **Senior Subordinated** tranche (Series K): 5.606% due 2039 at +138 bps to UST 4.375% due May 15, 2034.

### Broadcom Inc. (AVGO) — 2034 Tranche (Priced September 26, 2024)

| Tranche | Amount | Coupon | Maturity | Spread Over Benchmark Treasury | Benchmark |
|---------|--------|--------|----------|-------------------------------|-----------|
| 4.800% Senior Notes due 2034 | $1,750M | 4.800% | October 15, 2034 | **+103 bps** | UST 3.875% due August 15, 2034 |

### Difference Calculation

Assuming the question refers to BK's **largest senior note tranche (the $1.1B 5.060% Senior Notes due 2032)** with a spread of **+90 bps** to its benchmark treasury:

**103 bps − 90 bps = 13.00 basis points**

If instead the question refers to BK's 2028 fixed/floating senior notes (+65 bps), the difference would be **38.00 bps**. If referring to the floating rate senior notes (+83 bps to SOFR), the difference would be **20.00 bps** (though the benchmarks are not directly comparable).

The most reasonable interpretation given the context (comparing a fixed-rate spread over treasury to another fixed-rate spread over treasury) is the **+90 bps** spread on the 2032 senior notes, yielding a difference of **13.00 basis points**.

