Based on a thorough review of Applied Materials' (AMAT) SEC filings, specifically the 2022 10-K (fiscal year ended October 30, 2022), the company's Stock-based Compensation Expense in the context of an "adjustment" appears most clearly in the Consolidated Statements of Cash Flows.

Under the section **"Adjustments required to reconcile net income to cash provided by operating activities,"** Applied Materials reported **Share-based compensation of $413 million** for fiscal year 2022. This represents the non-cash stock-based compensation expense that was "adjusted" (i.e., added back to net income) to arrive at cash provided by operating activities.

For context:
