Based on an exhaustive review of UnitedHealth Group's SEC filings for 2020, **UnitedHealth Group did not report any adjustment to its Stock-based Compensation Expense in 2020.**

## Detailed Findings:

### Stock-Based Compensation Expense Reported (from 2020 10-K, Note 11):
| Year | Before Tax | Net of Tax |
|------|-----------|------------|
| 2020 | $679 million | $619 million |
| 2019 | $697 million | $641 million |
| 2018 | $638 million | $587 million |

### What I Searched:
1. **2020 10-K (filed March 1, 2021)** — Note 11 (Share-Based Compensation), Note 2 (Accounting Policies), MD&A, and the full document were searched for any mention of adjustments, modifications, changes in estimate, incremental expense, true-ups, reversals, or catch-up adjustments related to stock-based compensation. No such adjustment was disclosed.

2. **2019 10-K & 2021 10-K** — Checked for any retrospective disclosure or restatement of 2020 stock-based compensation figures. None found.

3. **2021 Proxy Statement (DEF 14A)** — The CD&A explicitly states: *"The Company did not change its performance targets for any of its executive compensation plans as a result of COVID-19."* No adjustments to stock-based compensation expense were discussed.

4. **Q1 and Q3 2020 10-Qs** — No adjustments to share-based compensation were reported.

5. **8-K filings from 2020** — No relevant disclosures about stock-based compensation adjustments.

### Year-over-Year Change:
The stock-based compensation expense changed from $697 million (2019) to $679 million (2020), representing a decrease of **$18 million** (approximately 2.58%). However, this is a standard year-over-year fluctuation and was not characterized by the company as an "adjustment."

### Conclusion:
UnitedHealth Group did not make or disclose any specific adjustment to its stock-based compensation expense in 2020. The reported expense of $679 million reflects the standard, recurring non-cash charge related to the company's compensation plans, with no modifications, catch-ups, or special adjustments disclosed.

