For the 2021 Performance Share Unit (PSU) awards, Everest Group, Ltd. (formerly Everest Re Group, Ltd., NYSE: RE, now NYSE: EG) established a **target of 10.5%** annual BVPS growth for the **2022 performance period**. 

According to the company's 2023 Proxy Statement (DEF 14A), the actual BVPS growth achieved in 2022 was **2.8%**, which fell below even the **threshold of 5.5%** (resulting in a 0% award multiplier and zero PSUs earned for this metric tranche).

### Basis Point Calculation

| Metric | Value | In Basis Points |
|--------|-------|-----------------|
| Target BVPS Growth (2022 Period) | 10.50% | 1,050 bps |
| Actual BVPS Growth (2022 Period) | 2.80% | 280 bps |
| **Difference** | **-7.70%** | **-770 bps** |

The 2022 BVPS growth fell short of the 10.5% target by **770 basis points** (i.e., the actual was 770 basis points below the target).

### Context
- For the PSU calculation, BVPS is defined as tangible book value per share under GAAP, but **excluding any adjustment for dividends paid to shareholders** (per the proxy statement).
- While the standard GAAP BVPS declined from $258.21 at year-end 2021 to $215.54 at year-end 2022 (a 16.5% decline per the 10-K), the PSU-specific calculation (which adds back dividends) yielded the 2.8% growth figure certified by the Compensation Committee.

