- 2019 10-K (filed Feb 28, 2020)
- 2018 10-K (filed Feb 28, 2019)
- 2023 10-K (filed Feb 23, 2024)
- 2024 10-K (filed Feb 27, 2025)
- Q3 2022 10-Q (filed Nov 3, 2022)

None of these filings mention any convertible notes, convertible debt, or convertible bonds. The company's senior notes (aggregate principal of $2.75 billion as of December 31, 2022) are all fixed-rate, non-convertible debt instruments. The company's preferred shares (Series F and Series G) are explicitly described as "not convertible into any other securities."

The only convertible securities Arch Capital Group has had in its history were **Series D convertible non-voting common equivalent preferred shares**, which were issued in connection with the AIG/United Guaranty acquisition in 2016. Each Series D Preferred Share converted to 10 common shares (representing up to 38,288,460 common shares), but **all Series D Preferred Shares were fully converted and no longer outstanding as of December 31, 2018** — well before the end of 2022.

Since Arch Capital Group had no convertible notes outstanding, the number of shares by which convertible notes could dilute the company by the end of 2022 is **zero (0)**.

