## Maximum Share Dilution from Paychex's Convertible Notes as of December 31, 2021

**Answer: 0.00% (No convertible notes exist)**

Based on a thorough review of Paychex Inc.'s (PAYX) SEC filings around December 31, 2021 — including the 10-K for the fiscal year ended May 31, 2021 (filed July 16, 2021), the 10-Q for the period ended August 31, 2021 (filed October 1, 2021), the 10-Q for the period ended November 30, 2021 (filed December 22, 2021), and the 10-Q for the period ended February 28, 2022 (filed March 31, 2022) — **Paychex did not have any convertible notes outstanding as of December 31, 2021.**

### Key Findings:

1. **No convertible notes or convertible debt exist in any filing.** A comprehensive search of all filings for terms including "convertible," "convertible notes," "convertible debt," "conversion," "exchangeable," "call option," "capped call," "hedge," and "warrant" returned no relevant results.

2. **Paychex's only long-term debt consisted of $800 million in Senior Notes (private placement debt):**
   - Senior Notes, Series A: $400 million at 4.07% fixed rate, maturing March 13, 2026
   - Senior Notes, Series B: $400 million at 4.25% fixed rate, maturing March 13, 2029
