Based on my comprehensive review of Honeywell International Inc.'s SEC filings, **Honeywell had 0 outstanding convertible notes at the end of 2020**, meaning they could potentially dilute 0 shares.

## Research Methodology and Findings:

I conducted an extensive search of Honeywell's (ticker: HON) SEC filings spanning multiple years to identify any convertible notes or convertible debt instruments. The search included:

### 10-K Annual Reports Reviewed:
- **2020 10-K** (filed 2021-02-12, report date 2020-12-31): The word "convertible" does not appear anywhere in this document. All debt instruments disclosed were standard Senior Notes, Euro Notes, Floating Rate Notes, Debentures, and Credit Agreements - none with conversion features.

