**Answer: The average number of broker non-votes per Annual Meeting for Consolidated Edison, Inc. (NYSE: ED) across the six-year period from May 20, 2019 to May 20, 2024 was 60,360,668.00.**

## Step-by-Step Calculation

Broker non-votes are reported in the 8-K filings following each annual meeting for all non-routine proposals (election of directors, advisory vote on executive compensation, and any other non-routine proposals). The ratification of independent accountants is a routine proposal under NYSE rules, so it carries no broker non-votes.

| Year | Annual Meeting Date | Broker Non-Votes |
|------|---------------------|------------------|
| 2019 | May 20, 2019 | 77,695,958 |
| 2020 | May 18, 2020 | 64,677,165 |
| 2021 | May 17, 2021 | 58,303,421 |
| 2022 | May 16, 2022 | 54,783,753 |
| 2023 | May 15, 2023 | 53,359,599 |
| 2024 | May 20, 2024 | 53,344,112 |

**Sum:** 77,695,958 + 64,677,165 + 58,303,421 + 54,783,753 + 53,359,599 + 53,344,112 = **362,164,008**

**Average:** 362,164,008 ÷ 6 = **60,360,668.00**

The broker non-votes declined steadily year-over-year, from approximately 77.7 million in 2019 to 53.3 million in 2024.

