Based on my thorough review of the Corning Incorporated (NYSE: GLW) filings, specifically the DEF 14A Proxy Statement filed on March 17, 2023 (which is referenced by the 8-K/A signed on June 22, 2023), I was unable to identify specific costs that were **excluded** from the "Total All Other Compensation" column and instead reported as perquisites for Wendell P. Weeks.

Instead, the proxy statement shows that all perquisites provided to Wendell P. Weeks were actually **included within** the "All Other Compensation" column of the Summary Compensation Table. For 2022, his "All Other Compensation" totaled **$475,185**, which included the following perquisites:

| Perquisite Category | Amount |
|---|---|
| Value of Personal Aircraft Rights | $207,133 |
| Value of Home Security Costs and Financial Counseling | $157,934 |
| Other (executive physicals, travel costs, annual Board gift, Corning Foundation Matching Gifts contributions) | $14,215 |

The proxy statement explicitly states: "Capped personal aircraft rights, financial counseling services and home security are the only perquisites offered to the NEOs."

One notable disclosure relates to the **valuation methodology** for personal aircraft usage: "Fixed costs that do not change based on usage, such as pilot salaries, hangar expense and general taxes and insurance, are excluded" from the calculation of the incremental cost. However, these fixed costs are excluded from the **valuation** of the perquisite — not excluded from the "All Other Compensation" column and reported elsewhere as perquisites.

Footnote (4)(iv) also addresses Mr. Weeks' security costs: "This reflects Company-paid expenses relating to personal and residential security benefitting Mr. Weeks and, through association, his family. Mr. Weeks' personal safety and security are of vital importance to the Company's business and prospects, and the Board considers these costs to be appropriate. However, because these costs can be viewed as conveying a personal benefit to Mr. Weeks, they are reported as perquisites in this column."

In summary, the proxy statement does not describe any costs that were excluded from the "Total All Other Compensation" column and instead reported separately as perquisites. All perquisites were included within that column as line items.

