## CenterPoint Energy (CNP) Louisiana RSP Filing — COVID-19 Bad Debt Cost Recoveries

In its September 2022 Louisiana Rate Stabilization Plan (RSP) filing with the Louisiana Public Service Commission (LPSC), CenterPoint Energy sought to recover specific regulatory assets related to incremental COVID-19 bad debt expenses. The filing included the following cost recoveries:

- **North Louisiana: $0.7 million** in COVID-19 bad debt expense regulatory assets
- **South Louisiana: $0.3 million** in COVID-19 bad debt expense regulatory assets

These COVID-19 bad debt recoveries were part of a broader RSP filing that sought a total annual increase of approximately $7 million ($3 million for North Louisiana and $5 million for South Louisiana), based on a Return on Equity (ROE) of 9.95% with a 50 basis point (+/-) earnings band and a test year ended June 2022.

### Outcome

On **April 5, 2023**, the LPSC issued an order approving a joint settlement for the RSP filing. The approved settlement provided **$2.7 million** for North Louisiana and **$4.6 million** for South Louisiana for the base rate increases, and critically, the LPSC order approved **the full impacts of the COVID-19 recoveries**—meaning the full $0.7 million and $0.3 million amounts sought were authorized for recovery. The new rates were implemented in May 2023.

### Follow-up (September 2023 RSP Filing)

A subsequent Louisiana RSP filing was made in September 2023 seeking an additional $10 million annual increase. This later filing explicitly referenced the **"completion of COVID-19 asset recovery"** — indicating that the COVID-19 bad debt regulatory assets ($0.7 million North Louisiana and $0.3 million South Louisiana) had been fully recovered through rates by that time.

